      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "AIM",
          "content": "To analyze prevalence of ischemic heart disease (IHD), main IHD risk factors and mortality in the population of males aged 70-79 and over 80 years."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "MATERIALS AND METHODS",
          "content": "The study included 209 males aged 70-79 years and 96 males over 80. All the males were examined for IHD and 3 main risk factors: blood hypertension, hyperlipidemia and smoking."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Incidence of IHD was about similar in both age groups. For 3.5 years of follow-up in the group of 80-year-olds mortality was 2 times that of the group of 70-79-year-olds. The presence of IHD in the groups was directly related to the presence of 2 or 3 risk factors, especially in the group aged 70-79 years. In the group of 80-year-olds and older combination of IHD with affection of cerebral vessels was a poor prognosis sign."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Factors deteriorating prognosis in males over 70 were: macrofocal myocardial infarction in anamnesis, atherosclerosis of the coronary and cerebral arteries."
        }
      ]},
